CONVERSATION:
Yeah, another one of these, I know.

    So me and my girlfriend have been dating for nearly two years now. We started dating in junior year of high school, and thigs were great. I love her very much, and I know she feels the same. We&apos;ve even discussed marriage/moving in after college.

    But recently, I don&apos;t know if she&apos;s the right one for me. Here&apos;s the full story...

    So, all through freshman year, and up until now, I&apos;ve had a crush on a girl. We&apos;ve stayed friends, and junior year my best friend starts dating her. I never even hinted at trying to break them up due to my feelings, and I let it go. I knew I would never date her, so I gave up trying. Cue my current relationship. So, things were great for the next year and a half. Senior year graduation, my best friend is having a grad party. I go with my girl, and his is there. This is no problem, we stayed friends like I said. We were drinking and stuff, it was generally a great time. Party ends, and I go home. I get a text from his girl, and it leads to us sexting and sending pics and talking about hookups. I text her for a few days, then she decides she doesn&apos;t like it and tells my girlfriend about the pics. Naturally, she was extremely upset. I promised her it would never happen again, and it didn&apos;t. But for the next few months things were kind of weird. We were arguing a lot more, and it seemed she just wasn&apos;t happy.

    She goes to college right by my house, and she lives there. There&apos;s a guy that works there, name is unimportant. So things were going pretty good for a few months, then a friendship develops between her and this guy. Nothing too out of the ordinary, and he was a pretty cool guy, and it turned into a mutual friendship for all of us.

    Few months after we started talking to this guy, he texts her asking if she was single would they hook up, etc. And this is right at the time we&apos;re having more problems. She tells me we need to take a break, and we can hook up with others during the break. I didn&apos;t, because I knew the shitstorm that would ensue, and I&apos;m a halfway decent guy, so I didn&apos;t want/need to. She is different. Less than 24 hours after, she fucks him. She tells me about her crush on him, and how attracted she is to him, etc. We end up getting back together, and neither of us talk to him anymore. As far as I know, she doesn&apos;t even know what she saw in him.

    But after all of this, I&apos;m left feeling like the problems that occurred in this relationship would be too much for me to overlook. The way she acts, how she responds to stress, everything. I love her so much, but I&apos;m still feeling like this relationship is basically over, and the longer we stay with each other, the more harmful it is to both of us.

    I come here and post this because it&apos;s impossible for me to get objective stands on this. Everyone I&apos;ve tried talking to is biased towards me, and tells me that she was wrong, shes a slut, I should leave her. But I don&apos;t want to. I love her, and want to stay with her. But I don&apos;t know if it&apos;s healthy for either of us.

    Sorry for the TL;DR post, and thanks for listening.
