CONVERSATION:
hi ppl
I uploaded my project (or whatever little is a start) to SourceForge (got a headache from trying to figure out Subversion, I used to use CVS long time ago but I dunno how well I did with SVN)
there might be mistakes that could conflict with other javascript libs. If anyone wants to fix those, I'd be thankful for the help
I chose the name Fiks.html for now (if anybody remembers, it's a script to make current browsers display HTML 5 correctly)
I guess Fiks kind of works the best, and I omitted the O since I didn't have anywhere to put it, and Opera can be considered the least broken (it supports Web Forms 2.0 after all =) )
if anybody wants to take a look, here's the SVN repo: http://fikshtml.svn.sourceforge.net/viewvc/fikshtml/
I'm kinda getting the feeling I either get on when everyone's asleep, or whatwg might be the more appropriate room?
i was responding to feedback on the list :-)
looks cool
you'll probably get more people on board once you've done a lot more work
people seem to ignore people's ideas until those people have shown that they can actually do what they want to do :-)
just look at the whatwg/html5 stuff, the amount of people who were interested in it has been directly proportional to how much work the people already involved had done so far
well, my current todo list on the project isn't that much anyway. Just fix the display of new elements and changed elements
and maybe the DOM
cool
but I don't want to reinvent the wheel with Web Forms 2.0 because it's already been done. A better solution would be to get it to integrate well with those existing projects
I started my project becasue I haven't seen one like it already
yeah integrating with the existing wf2 projects (and maybe breathing more life into them) would be great
I'm having trouble visualizing some of the other new elements such as meter though. I kinda doubt I'll implement it how it's meant to be (and that includes DOM, not only display), so I wanted to get more info from people on that b4 I tried
my current work was extracted from a real life project and cleaned up. I usually don't work on things I'm not using yet, let alone, can't visualize all the way yet
&lt;meter&gt; is basically a gauge
yeah, but it can be circular, linear, look like a existing colntrol, or just a shiney bar, or anything
like as in http://developer.apple.com/documentation/UserExperience/Conceptual/AppleHIGuidelines/XHIGControls/chapter_19_section_5.html#//apple_ref/doc/uid/TP30000359-DontLinkElementID_74
yeah the look isn't well-defined, but that's partially intentional, to allow people to experiment and find good looks and looks that fit well with their platform
oh, I see. but that raises some interesting questions: will the browsers make it look somewhat similar (I can imagine IE being the only one with a pie chart style)? and will the users be able to customize the look with CSS? will that introduce a bunch of -moz-meter-style attributes?
we'll probably standardise on default dimensions pretty soon after the browsers start implementing it
much like the form controls have de-facto default dimensions
as for styling, i don't know
maybe XBL2 will save us :-)
how about &lt;audio&gt; and &lt;video&gt; anybody tried making a script to implement that in current browsers?
some of the new browsers already have that so I don't know if that's worth implementing for older browsers or not
is there a fallback method for those tags? &lt;video&gt;&lt;embed&gt;&lt;/video&gt;?
for the time element, does it show the datetime as a tooltip?
well, that one actually seems as though it's not a stable part of the spec, so I guess I won't do that one yet
yeah &lt;video&gt;&lt;embed&gt;&lt;/video&gt; is the idea
&lt;time&gt; could show the time as a tooltip
doesn't have to though
well, I think it've that that did be able to customize the look, and did be able to make a script to implement that in current browsers????????????? did be able to make a script to figure that one yet've that that did be able to make a script to implement that in current browsers???? did be able to make a script to figure that one yet've that that did be able to make a script to implement that in current browsers???? did be able to make a script to figure that did be able to make a head, and did be able to make a script to figure that did be"")
