CONVERSATION:
4c681049601b3c374f1d2c0077c99049: I hate to nitpick, but the description for GameBoy-Online is off in http://code.google.com/p/html5rocks/wiki/AudioLibraries
You don't port GameBoyCore to HTML5
It's a hardware (CPU+LCD+SOUND+SERIAL) emulator of the GameBoy Color hardware.
:P
It's not a port of anything
The code is actually all mine
except the boot rom, because, you know, it's the actual boot rom used internally on the nintendo GameBoy Color.
I converted the bin dump by costis to a javascript friendly hex array for that. :P
The boot rom that was supposed to be un-dumpable
and dumped in fall '09
Way later than the GBA dump, because the boot rom hid itself from the memory map once the lockout register was tripped.
the GBA BIOS ROM just needed a subroutine to be exploited to be dumped, since it was still mapped, but blocked off from reading
so the trick there was for the GBA BIOS ROM to dump itself
by using a MIDI subroutine to read bytes of the boot rom memory, that nintendo forgot to block the BIOS from reading itself for.
:P
FTFY: making read-protected BIOS read itself out to homebrew ROMs. :P
but the GBC boot ROM needed manual hackery
to fuck up the CPU itself to not lock the boot ROM memory from the memory itself
Reading things that should not be possible to read. FTFY
--&gt; http://www.fpgb.org/?page_id=17
GBC boot ROM page of Costis
Extra &quot;yo dawg&quot; disassembly of it - http://www.its.caltech.edu/~costis/cgb_hack/gbc_bios.txt
WARNING: mind fuck for those that don't know assembly code.
You need to know how to work the stack and heap, just like C, but manually by hand. :P
and load the values into specific registers, manipulate them, and store them manually
:P
and you especially need to know the program counter, which C/C++ people don't usually need to deal with.
GB/GBC address registers are the SP, PC, and HL regs
since they're 16-bit
well
H and L are two 8-bit
but usually used together
There is also a high RAM zero-page speed opcode for accessing 0xFFXX with specifying only the lower byte.
:)
C can be compiled to GBC though
compiler - http://gbdk.sourceforge.net/
&lt;/spam&gt;
This should help reduce the mindfuck http://gameboy.mongenel.com/dmg/asmmemmap.html
:)
and http://gameboy.mongenel.com/dmg/opcodes.html
if you know 8080 assembly code, you might know some of this. :P
